# $egnet: ChangeLog,v 1.23 2005/03/18 02:48:07 dive Exp $

* 20030710/dive:
1) Started a changelog (Hi Trunks!) (everybody please use this format for
   changelog entries)
2) Merged in a (supposedly better) str_hash function
3) Merged in a change to free_activation that makes it take a pointer, not an
   entire activation structure

* 20030711/dive:
1) removed some prototypes from extensions.c, since they are properly prototyped
   in the includes.
2) have Makefile regen keywords.c from keywords.gperf, as this is still done by
   the sourceforge LambdaMOO project. Note that we don't include pgperf, so a
   dependency on gperf now exists. Most systems should have it, however the
   autoconf stuff needs to be fixed to check for it. Also note that committing
   from a working directory where we've built the server is no longer
   recommended, because keywords.c will change every time the server is built.
   (specifically, the rcsid will change, because its generated from
   keywords.gperf)
3) get rid of the Log keyword (and data after it) from configure.ac
4) remove some remnants of the old network checks from configure.ac.
   configure.ac could use a looking at anyway, as it has checks for things that
   have been obsolete for over a decade. (such as NeXT)
5) regen configure w/ autoconf
6) ran NetBSD's indent on every .[ch] file. This fixes indentation to how I like
   it: tabs, not spaces. Solved todo #8, which has thusly been removed.

* 20030715/dive:
1) added 'configure.lineno' to the list of files removed by 'make distclean' in
   Makefile.in. This file got leftover by configure on my NetBSD/alpha machine.

* 20040413/dive:
1) added Luke-Jr's patch for read_activ FUNC_NOT_FOUND (from lambdamoo sf
   project)
2) Many todo's solved. See commit logs for more information.
3) change FUP_version to 1.8p3 in version.c, because of the FUP fixes.

* 20050130/dive:
1) fixed some more compiler warnings (also remembered that we have a ChangeLog)

* 20050314/dive:
1) fixed the TODO entry re: function_info showing odd values to non-wizards
   for cmdlog_status.
2) Redid a lot of configure.ac; got rid of a ton of bitrot, and added a
   gperf check. Regen'd configure, in the process of testing now, so far
   things are going very well.
2) got rid of the strip step in Makefile.in. Anything with enough RAM for a
   MOO can handle the overhead.
3) Fixed configure.ac (and regen'd configure again) so that it will bomb if
   it can't find a yaccer or gperf.
4) Fixed a bug I accidentally introduced with change #1 from today.

* 20050315/dive
1) removed ref_count.c, malloc.c
2) regen'd Makefile.in
3) regen'd configure
4) removed char rcsid_foo[] from all C files (no need for the extra bloat)

* 20050317/dive
1) fixed improper usage of AC_CHECK_PROGS(... yacc ...) in configure.ac
2) regen'd configure
